		EXEMPLE OF CONFIGURATION
        =======================
		
	<LIVERY_OVERRIDE LIVERY="51" NAME="Custom" BASELIVERY="BluInfinito">
	  <PREVIEWIMAGE PATH="\Custom livery.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="VINYL" PATH="\Vinyls\performance_livery.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="BADGES" PATH="\Badges\black.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="CALIPERS" PATH="\Calipers\nero.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="INTERIORDIFF" PATH="\Interior\interior_black_diff.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="INTERIORSPEC" PATH="\Interior\interior_black_spec.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="ALCANTARA" PATH="\Interior\alcantara_black.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="WHEELDIFF" PATH="\Rims\black_diff.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="WHEELSPEC" PATH="\Rims\black_spec.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="WHEELBLURDIFF" PATH="\Rims\black_blur_diff.dds" />
	  <TEXTURE NAME="WHEELBLURDIFF" PATH="\Rims\black_blur_spec.dds" />
    </LIVERY_OVERRIDE>
						
						
						TIREDIFF	- tire_diff - Tire branding texture
                                    - 1024 x 1024
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs
									
						TIRESPEC	- tire spec_diff - Tire branding texture
                                    - 1024 x 1024
                                    - DXT5 with MIPs
									
					TIREBLURDIFF	- tire_blur_diff - Tire branding texture
                                    - 1024 x 1024
                                    - DXT5 with MIPs
									
					TIREBLURSPEC	- tire_blur_spec - Tire branding texture
                                    - 1024 x 1024
                                    - DXT5 with MIPs
									
					TIRENORM		- tire_normal_map - Tire branding texture
                                    - 1024 x 1024
                                    - DXT5 with MIPs
									
		HELMETS
        =======================

        For each overriden livery a helmet override can be defined. The work similarly to liveries
        in that they override a named base helmet with user defined textures. To assigne a helmet
        to a livery use the same 'LIVERY' id as in the livery override

        AVAILABLE BASE HELMETS
        =======================

				DEFAULT: default helmet used by all vehicles of the class
                Available textures: 
                        BODY        - the main exterior surface of the helmet
                                    - 2048 x 2048
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs
                        						
						VISOR     	- visor texture
                                    - 2048 x 2048
                                    - DXT5 with MIPs
									
		OUTFITS
        =======================

        As with helmets, they work similarly to liveries in that they override a named base part with user defined textures. To assigne a part
        to a livery use the same 'LIVERY' id as in the livery override

        AVAILABLE BASE OUTFITS
        =======================

				DEFAULT: default helmet used by all vehicles of the class
                Available textures: 
                        BODY_DIFF   - the main exterior surface of the helmet
                                    - 2048 x 2048
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs
                        						
						ARMS_DIFF 	- visor texture
                                    - 2048 x 1024
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs

                        GLOVES_DIFF - the main exterior surface of the helmet
                                    - 2048 x 2048
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs
                        						
						LEGS_DIFF 	- visor texture
                                    - 2048 x 1024
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs

                     SEATBELTS_DIFF - the main exterior surface of the helmet
                                    - 2048 x 2048
                                    - DXT1 with MIPs
										

